 "raw_reply": "{\"item\": \"S445-017\", \"clauses\": {\"estimate_capacity\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F06\", \"template\": \"{article} {target_noun}'s {mc_lbl} measures {val} {unit}. About how many {unit} is that, rounded to the nearest {round_to}?\", \"reasoning\": \"F06 asks the learner to estimate the capacity of a container or object by rounding its measured value to the nearest 10, which is an estimation task on capacity. The question_text field of F06 carries the 'About how many' estimate.\"}, \"liters_and_or_milliliters\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F06\", \"template\": \"{article} {target_noun}'s {mc_lbl} measures {val} {unit}. About how many {unit} is that, rounded to the nearest {round_to}?\", \"reasoning\": \"The unit slot of F06 draws from the generator's repeated unit values, printed as L and mL, so the same template produces problems in liters and in milliliters.\"}}, \"failing_families\": [\"F06\"], \"failing_templates\": [\"{article} {target_noun}'s {mc_lbl} measures {val} {unit}. About how many {unit} is that, rounded to the nearest {round_to}?\"], \"overall\": \"FAIL\", \"reasoning\": \"The article slot of F06 has the members A and An, and the target_noun slot has the members container and object. Both are derived only from measurement_type, and the domains state no joint constraint between them. The domains therefore allow the pairings An with container and A with object, and each produces ungrammatical learner text (An container's; A object's). Since the pairing is not fixed by the domains, a grade 3 learner can be shown an incorrect statement, so the family fails Rule 1. F02, F03, F04 and F05 print only hint text whose slots are numbers from the observed runs, the unit values L and mL, and the answers 10 to 70 in steps of 10. Their templates use no vocabulary outside cumulative_vocab (halfway and rounds up are plain-language wording with round in the cumulative list). F04 and F05 omit the unit, which is less clear but not wrong, so they are not failing. F01 prints only the cumulative word capacity. No NOT_YET_KNOWN term appears in any template or domain.\"}",
